      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Tanglewilds rainforest"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A swarm of tiny iridescent wasps with blue-green thoraxes and dark reddish abdomens. They cluster around a concealed hardened mud nest."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Senses",
          "lines": [
            "Blindsight 10 ft."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Damage resistances",
          "lines": [
            "Bludgeoning",
            "Piercing",
            "Slashing",
            "Fire"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Condition immunities",
          "lines": [
            "Charmed",
            "Frightened",
            "Grappled",
            "Paralyzed",
            "Petrified",
            "Prone",
            "Restrained",
            "Stunned"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Attacks",
          "lines": [
            "Sting · Melee Weapon Attack · +3 to hit · 4d4 poison"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Traits mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Swarm · The swarm can share spaces with other creatures and move through a gap large enough for one Tiny insect. It cannot regain HP or gain temporary HP.",
            "Wrong Step · The swarm surrounds a 1-ft. ball of hardened mud in a 5-ft. space. Spotting the concealed nest takes a DC 17 Wisdom (Perception) check. A creature that steps on the nest is grappled on a failed save (escape DC 14). The nest can grapple only one creature. While grappled, the creature takes 5 (2d4) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. Another creature within reach of the nest can spend an action to free it with a DC 14 Strength (Athletics) check. · DC 14 Strength · 2d4 poison (start of grappled target turn)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Actions mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Sting · +3 to hit · One target in the swarm's space (0-ft. reach) takes 10 (4d4) poison damage on a hit, or 5 (2d4) when the swarm is at half HP or fewer. · 4d4 poison (above half HP) · 2d4 poison (half HP or fewer)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "The stat block prints a single 30-ft. speed. The reference art depicts winged insects.",
            "The night travel table on p. 7 calls for a DC 17 group Wisdom (Perception) check to avoid disturbing nests and provoking 2d6 swarms.",
            "Hit Point Press, The Heart of Dako, p. 25, and reference cards, p. 10."
          ]
        }
      ],
